{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception and actuation interface, separating sensor outcomes (uncontrollable) from motion commands (controllable). The specification encodes a safe, always-turn-right exploration policy: move forward when clear, rotate clockwise to recover from any obstacle, and never enable forward motion when an obstacle is detected. Recovery states only allow rotate_clockwise, and return to forward progress as soon as the path is clear.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for sensing/actuation and for specification/policy.",
    "Specification ensures safety (no forward on obstacle) and progress (prefer move_forward, always turn right for recovery)."
  ],
